# wimirage — Architecture

A Mermaid.js rendering of the runtime topology for `wimirage` v2.x.
Render with any Mermaid-compatible viewer (`mermaid-cli`, GitHub,
Obsidian, mkdocs-material, etc.).

---

## 1. High-level runtime

```mermaid
flowchart LR
    subgraph Operator
        CLI[main.py menu loop]
    end

    subgraph "core/"
        AC[AttackContext]
        EB[EventBus]
        PM[ProcessManager]
        SC[APScanner]
        DA[DeauthAttack]
        RA[RogueAP]
        NC[NetworkConfig]
        CP[CaptivePortal]
        OTP[OTPServiceInterface<br/><i>Demo / Twilio</i>]
    end

    subgraph "utils/"
        MM[MonitorMode]
        CL[CredentialLogger]
        CU[Cleanup]
        RETRY[@retry decorator]
    end

    subgraph "portal/"
        BP[Flask Blueprint<br/>routes.py]
        T[(templates/)]
        S[(static/)]
    end

    subgraph "host OS"
        HOSTAPD[hostapd]
        DNSMASQ[dnsmasq]
        IPT[iptables]
        SCAPY[scapy sniff/sendp]
        FS[(logs/*.jsonl<br/>logs/audit.log)]
    end

    CLI -->|owns| AC
    AC --> SC & DA & RA & NC & CP & EB & PM
    CP -->|mounts| BP
    BP -->|reads| T & S
    CP --> OTP

    SC --> SCAPY
    DA --> SCAPY
    RA --> PM
    PM --> HOSTAPD & DNSMASQ
    RA --> HOSTAPD
    NC --> IPT

    CL --> FS
    CL -.->|Fernet optional| FS
    EB --> CP

    DA -.uses.-> RF[perf_counter<br/>drift-free PPS]
    SC -.uses.-> BATCH[queue.Queue<br/>+ batch worker]
    CL -.uses.-> BF[batched JSONL flush]
    CU -.uses.-> RETRY
    CU -.installs.-> SIG[SIGINT/SIGTERM handler]
```

