## 2. State machine

```mermaid
stateDiagram-v2
    [*] --> IDLE

    IDLE --> SCANNING
    SCANNING --> SCANNED
    SCANNING --> IDLE

    SCANNED --> TARGET_SELECTED
    SCANNED --> SCANNING

    TARGET_SELECTED --> DEAUTH_RUNNING
    TARGET_SELECTED --> SCANNING

    DEAUTH_RUNNING --> AP_RUNNING
    DEAUTH_RUNNING --> TARGET_SELECTED

    AP_RUNNING --> PORTAL_RUNNING
    AP_RUNNING --> DEAUTH_RUNNING

    PORTAL_RUNNING --> IDLE
    FULL_ATTACK --> IDLE
    FULL_ATTACK --> PORTAL_RUNNING

    note right of FULL_ATTACK
        Menu option 7 — end-to-end chain.
        Transitions to PORTAL_RUNNING
        when the user stops the deauth
        or the OTP alone mode is entered.
    end note

    IDLE --> [*]
```

---

## 3. Full attack chain (data flow)

```mermaid
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant O as Operator
    participant M as main.py / MenuHandler
    participant S as Scanner
    participant D as DeauthAttack
    participant R as RogueAP
    participant N as NetworkConfig
    participant P as CaptivePortal
    participant V as Victim
    participant O2 as OTPService

    O->>M: menu option 7 — full attack chain
    M->>S: enable_monitor + sniff (20s)
    S-->>M: list[AccessPoint]
    O->>M: pick target AP
    M->>D: start(target_bssid, channel)
    D-->>M: background thread @ PPS

    M->>R: start(ssid, channel)
    R-->>M: hostapd + dnsmasq up

    M->>N: setup_iptables()<br/>(NAT + redirect :80/53)
    N-->>M: OK

    M->>P: start()
    P-->>M: serving on :80

    loop victim flow
        V->>P: connect to SSID, GET /
        P-->>V: login.html (csrf_token)
        V->>P: POST /submit (csrf, phone, email)
        P->>O2: generate_otp + send_otp
        O2-->>V: SMS or demo print
        V->>P: POST /verify (otp)
        P-->>V: success.html (if valid)
        P->>N: grant_internet(client_ip)
    end

    O->>M: Ctrl+C
    M->>P: stop()
    M->>R: stop() (hostapd, dnsmasq)
    M->>D: stop()
    M->>N: cleanup() (flush iptables, disable forwarding)
    M->>S: enable_monitor(None)
```

---

## 4. Module boundaries

```mermaid
flowchart TB
    subgraph "core/ (domain)"
        direction TB
        M[models.py<br/>dataclasses + enums]
        E[events.py]
        PM2[process_manager.py]
        SC2[scanner.py]
        DE[deauth.py]
        RA2[rogue_ap.py]
        NE[network.py]
        CP2[captive_portal.py]
        OT2[otp_service.py]
    end

    subgraph "utils/ (adapters)"
        direction TB
        U1[monitor_mode.py]
        U2[logger.py]
        U3[cleanup.py]
    end

    subgraph "portal/ (HTTP layer)"
        direction TB
        R1[routes.py<br/>build_portal_blueprint]
        R2[templates/*.html]
        R3[static/*.{js,css}]
    end

    CP2 -.lazy import.-> R1
    R1 --> CP2
    R1 --> R2
    R1 --> R3

    RA2 --> PM2
    NE --> U3
    OT2 --> U2
    DE --> SCAPY2[scapy]
    SC2 --> SCAPY2
    U3 -.->|SIGINT/SIGTERM| NE
```

### Boundary rules

- **`core/` ↛ `utils/`.** A small number of `utils.cleanup` functions are
  called from `core.network` (`flush_iptables`). All other `core`
  modules must not import from `utils/`.
- **`portal/routes.py` not importable from `core/`.** The lazy import
  inside `build_portal_blueprint()` is the contract — do not move it
  to the module top.
- **`utils/` ↛ `core/`** when there's an obvious lower-level alternative.
  For instance, `Cleanup` calls the standalone `flush_iptables()`
  helper in `core/network.py`, not `NetworkConfig.flush_iptables()`
  (which would create state). Subprocess-layer adapters in `utils/`
  should reach for the lowest-level primitive they can.

---

## 5. Credential log pipeline

```mermaid
flowchart LR
    A[Portal route<br/>/submit /verify /resend]
    -->|log_credential| Q[threading Queue]
    -->|drain every 5s OR 10 entries| W[_flush_worker]
    -->|append + fsync| J[(captured_credentials.jsonl)]
    -->|Fernet optional| J

    L[RotatingFileHandler<br/>audit.log]
    -->|logger.critical/info/error| RH[10MB x 5 backups]

    classDef hot fill:#fdd,stroke:#900
    classDef store fill:#dfd,stroke:#070
    class A,Q hot
    class J,RH store
```

---

## 6. Plugin system (planned)

```mermaid
flowchart LR
    A[core.plugins<br/>registry.py]
    -->|scans entry points| EP[importlib.metadata.EntryPoint]
    EP --> PS[scanner plugins]
    EP --> PD[deauth plugins]
    EP --> PR[rogue_ap plugins]
    EP --> PO[otp plugins]

    SC[APScanner] --> A
    DA[DeauthAttack] --> A
    RA[RogueAP] --> A
    OT[OTPServiceInterface] --> A
```

Plugins let third parties swap a single attack-stage implementation
without forking the main project. Currently this is a sketch in
`plan5goal5.md` Section 2 #9 — code pending.

